## How to use this section

1. New contributors should read pages in the listed order.
2. Experienced contributors can jump straight to Templates and Publishing flow.
3. Reviewers should focus on publishing flow, templates, and ownership guidance.

## Minimum publishing readiness checklist

1. Content follows the repository structure and naming conventions.
2. Page metadata is complete and owner is clearly set.
3. Writing style is task-oriented and externally understandable.
4. Diagrams and images have sufficient context and accessibility support.
5. Local preview and link checks pass.
6. PR has reviewer sign-off from the owning team.

## Recommended documentation template

For teams creating a documentation site, use the MoJ template repository:

- [ministryofjustice/template-documentation-site](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/template-documentation-site)

This is the recommended baseline because it:

1. Uses GOV.UK technical docs patterns.
2. Supports local preview workflows.
3. Supports link validation workflows.
4. Provides a familiar structure for docs-as-code workflows.

